      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports impression management as a workplace tactic and says virtual-meeting fatigue can prompt the use of impression-management behaviors, but it does not support the broad general definition that it is the use of behaviors or communication features to shape how one is seen by others.",
        "The packet does not support the specific causal chain that heightened self-monitoring and facial-appearance concerns in virtual meetings contribute to fatigue in the way stated; it only says negative self-evaluation stemming from heightened self-monitoring is associated with Zoom fatigue and that facial-appearance dissatisfaction is associated with VM fatigue."
